  "plain": "In 1980s Las Vegas, Bob Lazar, a man who says he worked on alien craft at a secret Nevada base, met the aviator John Lear through a friend named Gene Huff, a property appraiser. Lazar tells it himself: Huff was doing the appraisal on Lear's house, and Lazar went along. It is how he tells the start of his ties to the circle that would later bring his story out."
